    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d388">

                <pb facs="0558" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg452"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister
                    Barrett.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-03-19"><hi rendition="#italic">March 19,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 16.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 41, of the 13th ultimo, in regard to the additional duty of 8 cents (making
                    a total of approximately 21 per kilogram) imposed on foreign flour.</p>
                <p>It would appear that the figures given by you state the duty in Colombian
                    currency. If so, the equivalent in American gold might be stated for greater
                    convenience.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
